1201: \n1202: \section{Rational bounds for the finite reversal}\label{app:rational-calculation}\n1203: This appendix proves the privacy bounds used in\n1204: Theorem~\ref{thm:strict-interior-counterexample}. We partition the first two\n1205: reference coordinates into rectangles and integrate over the third\n1206: coordinate exactly. Rational interval arithmetic then bounds both directed\n1207: profiles. The supplement~\cite{rational-supplement} contains the individual\n1208: logarithm brackets and unrounded interval expressions. Decimal values, where\n1209: given, are for orientation only.\n1210: \n1211: \subsection{Conditional tails and rectangle bounds}\n1212: Fix $E=2$, $T=3$, $\Delta=1$, and $\varepsilon=1/4$. The candidate\n1213: privacy variance $v=5/32$ corresponds to\n1214: \[\n1215:  \sigma^2=\frac{E^2v}{T}=\frac5{24},\qquad\n1216:  \mu=\frac\Delta\sigma=\sqrt{\frac{24}{5}}.\n1217: \]\n1218: Write $P=P_{2/3,\sqrt{5/24}}$, $Q=Q_{\sqrt{5/24}}$, $q=2/3$, and\n1219: $\alpha=e^{1/4}$. After standardization, the one-coordinate likelihood ratio\n1220: under the reference law is\n1221: \[\n1222:  r(z)=\frac13+\frac23\exp\left(\mu z-\frac{\mu^2}{2}\right).\n1223: \]
