### lem:binomial-propagation [641, 918]
639: half-rate case.\n640: \n641: \subsection{Propagation in the center}\n642: \begin{lemma}[Propagation of positivity]\label{lem:binomial-propagation}\n643: Fix $h>0$ and $0\leq\theta_1<\theta_2$. If\n644: $\Gamma_{E,T}(\theta_1,h)\geq0$, then\n645: $\Gamma_{E,T}(\theta_2,h)>0$.\n646: \end{lemma}\n647: \n648: \begin{proof}\n649: For $t\in\R$, put $k_\theta(t)=h\phi(h(t-\theta))$. For every integer $z$,\n650: \[\n651:  \Phi(h(z-\theta))-\Phi(-h\theta)=\int_0^z k_\theta(t)\,dt.\n652: \]\n653: Let $A_\theta$ be the expectation of the positive integrals and $B_\theta$\n654: the expectation of the absolute values of the negative integrals. Then\n655: $\Gamma_{E,T}(\theta,h)=A_\theta-B_\theta$, and\n656: \[\n657:  \frac{k_{\theta_2}(t)}{k_{\theta_1}(t)}\n658:  =\chi\exp\bigl(h^2(\theta_2-\theta_1)t\bigr),\n659:  \qquad\n660:  \chi=\exp\left(-\frac{h^2}{2}(\theta_2^2-\theta_1^2)\right)>0.\n661: \]
