916: \n917: \begin{proof}[Proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:rate-adaptive-center}]\n918: For $T>2E$, equation~\eqref{eq:binomial-low-boundary-strict} proves positivity\n919: at $\theta=c_{E,T}$, and Lemma~\ref{lem:binomial-propagation} extends it to\n920: larger centers. For $E<T<2E$, Lemma~\ref{lem:binomial-reflected-zero} gives\n921: positivity at zero, and the same propagation lemma handles every positive\n922: center. At $T=2E$, symmetry gives equality at zero and propagation gives\n923: strict positivity for $\theta>0$.\n924: \end{proof}\n925: \n926: \subsection{Strict comparison at the symmetric endpoint}\n927: At the symmetric endpoint of Theorem~\ref{thm:rate-adaptive-pointwise}, the\n928: full-batch threshold gives a tie. A slightly larger threshold already\n929: gives a strict improvement using the average alone.\n930: \n931: \begin{lemma}[Improving the threshold at half rate]\label{lem:strict-average-endpoint}\n932: Let $E\in\N_{>0}$, $a>0$, and $K\sim\operatorname{Binomial}(2E,1/2)$.\n933: Let $Q=\Normal(0,1)$, and let $P$ be the mixture whose conditional law\n934: given $K=k$ is $\Normal(ak/E,1)$. With $\varepsilon=a^2/2$,\n935: \[\n936:  H_{e^\varepsilon}(P, Q)\n937:  >\frac12-e^\varepsilon\overline\Phi(a).\n938: \]
